<zk xmlns:n="native" xmlns:ca="client/attribute">
	<n:h1>WCAG 2.1 - 1.4.13 content on hover or focus: collapsed navbar</n:h1>
	<label multiline="true">
		A collapsed navbar shows icons only, so hovering an item reveals its label
		beside it, and hovering a nav reveals its children.
		1. hover "Leaf navitem" - its label appears to the right of the icon
		2. press Esc without moving the mouse - the label disappears
		3. keep the mouse still - it must stay hidden
		4. move away, hover the item again - the label is back
		5. hover the first icon (the nav) and press Esc - its child list closes too
	</label>
	<separator/>
	<navbar id="navbar" orient="vertical" collapsed="true" width="60px" ca:aria-label="Collapsed nav">
		<nav id="navWithChildren" iconSclass="z-icon-home" label="Nav with children">
			<navitem id="navChild1" iconSclass="z-icon-home" label="Child 1"/>
			<navitem id="navChild2" iconSclass="z-icon-home" label="Child 2"/>
		</nav>
		<navitem id="leafItem" iconSclass="z-icon-star" label="Leaf navitem"/>
	</navbar>
	<separator height="80px"/>
	<button id="away" label="park the pointer here"/>
</zk>
